<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.hand.withdraws ~ the hand takes one lifted revision off the stage

`kahua withdraw <cid>` withdraws one lifted revision of the face's stage, an act signed under the face's root out of sealed custody (the lōkahi cap and the operator's grant). It runs on a person's hand alone: an AI seat proposes and stages, and its session never withdraws; no tool carries it. Every answer prints as JSON.

Under a pūlama the root signs at the pūlama's hand door, since the vessel there holds no face root: `terms=true` runs every gate and prints ONE stdout line (the one unsigned act its root signs) and opens no route; the pūlama's `sign '<terms>'` checks it and signs; `land='<answer>'` lands the signed record, where the door builds the act afresh and lands it only over a byte-equal body. Neither asks the passphrase on the vessel, and the host shim walks the pattern (`tools/lares-container.sh kahua lift|withdraw|carry`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ one-revision

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`one-revision` params=`cid/<cid> face/1 ~ withdraw one revision of the face's stage`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ cid · face · terms · land

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`cid` params=`takes/cid needs/required seat/1 as/<cid> ~ the revision cid to withdraw, as 'lares kahua get <title> history=true' names it`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ which face's stage this call reads or writes, by persona index (a whole number from 0); absent, the one face standing open or the worn face`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`terms` params=`~ print the one terms line a pūlama signs; opens no route; name it or land=, never both`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`land` params=`takes/answer ~ land the signed record from a pūlama's sign answer`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand` params=`who/hand key/face-root ~ signs under the face's root out of sealed custody; a person runs it at their own terminal, and an AI seat names the command`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ withdraw-needs-a-cid · kahua-hand-malformed · face-malformed

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`withdraw-needs-a-cid` params=`cure/[[face.hand.withdraws cid/<cid>]] ~ the door says 'withdraw: name a revision cid'`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-hand-malformed` params=`~ the pūlama's answer names the wrong kind, the wrong face, or both terms=true and land=stood on one line`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-malformed` params=`~ face= names a persona index, a whole number from 0`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ withdrawn · refused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`withdrawn` params=`exit/0 ~ the revision stands withdrawn; the door's answer prints as JSON`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`refused` params=`exit/1 ~ the door refused by name; the line carries its reason`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares kahua withdraw

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`handler/host spells/[[lares kahua withdraw]] ~ the terminal`>>
```

